            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As soon as I came across this recipe in the reviews I immediately set out to try it. Mixed this right up using my fav Coke Zero and I wasn't surprised at all when I found it... delightful! The best things come from simple yet creative ideas like this!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We make this A LOT in this house. Works just as well with diet cola/\"zero\" cola. Awesome with a scoop of ice cream, too.",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-29T12:49:27.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MAMALEIGH"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If you like cherry cola, you'll enjoy this! I use 1 teaspoon of grenadine, but you can adjust the amount to suit your taste.",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-17T16:03:00.033Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was great! It definately reminded me of a cherry coke AND a Shirley Temple, which was one of my childhood favorites. I used diet cola and two maraschino cherries....so refreshing and simple. I will be making this again! Thanks for sharing. :)",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-29T10:16:26.027Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RMSR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used one teaspoon of grenadine and three maraschino cherries, but didn't get that cherry coke flavour the other reviews raved about. Maybe because I used Coke Zero? I would use two teaspoons of grenadine next time... I prefer using Sprite, hence being a Shirley Temple (a little note... Try creme de menthe- the mint version of grenadine- in your Shirley Temple for a different twist).",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-24T11:42:43.703Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BellsD"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Whenever my brother &amp; I went out to a nice restaurant as kids, I got a Shirley Temple and Timmy got a Roy Rogers. We thought we were so cool 'cuz they were served in 'grown-up glasses'. Thanks for bringing such great, ancient memories back!",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-16T18:06:44.807Z"
